    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d907">

                <pb facs="1333" n="1319" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg1319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">895.00/11–548</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lovett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-11-05">November 5, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Draft Resolution on Korea<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d907-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>There is attached for your approval a draft resolution on Korea which has
                    received informal clearance from FE, O, UNA, EUR, and L, and from General
                    Wedemeyer for the Army.</p>
                <p>It is proposed that this text, which represents certain revisions by a
                    Departmental working group of a draft submitted by the United <pb facs="1334"
                        n="1320" xml:id="pg1320"/> States Delegation to the General Assembly,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d907-f2"/> be approved for transmittal to the Delegation as a
                    basis for negotiation with other delegations on this subject, it being
                    understood that the Delegation will have a reasonable margin of discretion in
                    coordinating this draft with the views of other delegations, but that any
                    substantive changes in its text will be cleared with the Department.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
